# Day 006 - Git and GitHub

## Learning Objectives

* Understand what Git is
* Understand what version control is
* Connect a local repository to GitHub
* Push code to GitHub

## What is Git?

Git is a version control system that tracks changes in files and projects.

## What is Version Control?

Version control allows developers to save project history and return to previous versions when needed.

## Commands Learned

git --version

git init

git add .

git commit -m "message"

git push

